<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
  <!--
  Recorder permissions: none are needed.

  Android recording is InAppScreenRecorder (Unity-side capture + InAppFrameEncoder), not the
  SmileSoft/MediaProjection plugin, so the whole permission block that shipped with that plugin
  was dead weight and has been removed:

    WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE              no-op — AndroidMinSdkVersion is 35, and MediaStoreSaver
                                        inserts the app's own media under scoped storage, which
                                        needs no permission (see MediaStoreSaver.java).
    RECORD_AUDIO / MODIFY_AUDIO_SETTINGS the recorder's audio is Unity's own mixed output, tapped
                                        via OnAudioFilterRead (AudioCaptureTap.cs). Nothing in
                                        this project opens the mic — there is no Microphone.Start
                                        or AudioRecord anywhere.
    FOREGROUND_SERVICE, _MEDIA_PROJECTION,
    _MICROPHONE, POST_NOTIFICATIONS     existed only for the SmileSoft foreground services that
                                        were removed below. Also worth keeping out: declaring a
                                        foreground service type obliges you to fill in Play
                                        Console's foreground-service declaration form.
    VIDEO_CAPTURE / AUDIO_CAPTURE       not grantable to normal apps at all (signature|privileged);
                                        they were never doing anything.

  If SmileSoft/MediaProjection recording is ever re-enabled on Android, restore this block and the
  two <service> declarations together — the plugin needs both.
  -->
  <application>
    <activity android:name="com.unity3d.player.UnityPlayerActivity" android:theme="@style/UnityThemeSelector">
      <intent-filter>
        <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
        <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
      </intent-filter>
      <meta-data android:name="unityplayer.UnityActivity" android:value="true" />
    </activity>
    <!--
        Removed: a second <activity android:name="com.unity3d.player.UnityPlayerGameActivity">
        block (Unity's GameActivity boilerplate, referencing @style/BaseUnityGameActivityTheme)
        was here from the plugin's sample manifest. This project uses the classic
        UnityPlayerActivity entry point, not GameActivity, so that style is never generated by
        this build and resource linking failed on it (see build error:
        "resource style/BaseUnityGameActivityTheme ... not found").
        -->
    <!--
    Removed: the two SmileSoft MediaProjection foreground services
    (ScreenRecorderForegroundService / ...Mic) and the androidx FileProvider that backed the
    plugin's Android share sheet.

    Nothing on Android reaches any of them anymore. Recording is InAppScreenRecorder, saving is
    MediaStoreSaver, and sharing hands the resulting MediaStore content:// URI straight to the OS
    share sheet (InAppScreenRecorder.ShareLastRecording) — a content URI from MediaStore needs no
    FileProvider. SmileSoft is now iOS-only (ReplayKit), and FileProvider is an Android-only API,
    so none of this affects the iOS build.

    The FileProvider is also what Google Play was rejecting: the plugin hardcodes the authority
    "com.SmileSoft.unityplugin.ScreenRecordProvider", authorities are globally unique across the
    Play catalog, and other developers shipping the same plugin already claimed it —
    "The following content provider authorities are in use by other developers".
    -->
  </application>
</manifest>